ted_at":"2024-01-25T15:24:02.776Z"},{"id":"qwftD3jNW","title":"Coming soon: Qiskit 1.0!","url":"https://medium.com/qiskit/coming-soon-qiskit-1-0-a8d59c3533a4","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/coming-soon-qiskit-1-0--qwftd3jnw","summary":"Qiskit 1.0 will be released in February 2024, marking a new phase of development focused on performance, stability, and usability. The release will bring improvements in speed and memory usage. Users will need to create a new virtual environment to install Qiskit 1.0, and there will be breaking changes that may require code modifications. Downstream projects and library maintainers will also need to adapt to Qiskit 1.0.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/9b4e16d2c6493bfa846e2239a52f0ef8?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-12-20T16:34:16.519Z"},{"id":"rvhRLDQuZ","title":"Qiskit 1.0 coming in February, 2024","url":"https://medium.com/qiskit/qiskit-1-0-coming-in-february-2024-6599b1724f0c","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/qiskit-1-0-coming-in-february-2024-rvhrldquz","summary":"Qiskit 1.0 is a major milestone in quantum computing, bringing performance, stability, and usability enhancements. It offers improved speed and memory usage, as well as a stable API. Upgrading to Qiskit 1.0 requires creating a new virtual environment.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/fada5f55f268662e9573698435165125?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-12-20T16:11:26.306Z"},{"id":"6gcbVQUy8","title":"A Christmas Closed-Timelike-Curve: Could the story of Scrooge actually happen in a quantum universe?","url":"https://medium.com/qiskit/a-christmas-closed-timelike-curve-could-the-story-of-scrooge-actually-happen-in-a-quantum-universe-cb22cdf8c9a7?source=rss----85f9df9eaa17---4","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/a-christmas-closed-timelike-curve-could-the-story-of-scrooge-actually-happen-in-a-quantum-universe--6gcbvquy8","summary":"The article explores the possibility of the story of Scrooge from 'A Christmas Carol' happening in a universe with quantum time-loops. It discusses the effects of the visits from the Ghost of Christmas Past and the Ghost of Christmas Present on Scrooge, and the paradox involving the Ghost of Christmas Yet-To-Come. The article also mentions the concept of self-consistency in resolving time-travel paradoxes.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/ac175071f8c32d239829328c70aa601c?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-12-13T18:05:11.916Z"},{"id":"BVJz2f9UB","title":"Coming soon: Qiskit 1.0!","url":"https://medium.com/qiskit/coming-soon-qiskit-1-0-9dac8ae16da7?source=rss----85f9df9eaa17---4","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/coming-soon-qiskit-1-0--bvjz2f9ub","summary":"Qiskit 1.0 is set to be released in February 2024 as a new phase of Qiskit development. It will focus on performance, stability, and usability. Users can expect a high-performance code base, a leaner package, and a more stable API. To upgrade to Qiskit 1.0, users need to create a new virtual environment and follow the provided instructions.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/9a88750a237cd9bdbd80551d0468bf64?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-11-30T15:57:21.861Z"},{"id":"7VnaOyqUO","title":"A new chapter for Qiskit algorithms and applications","url":"https://medium.com/qiskit/a-new-chapter-for-qiskit-algorithms-and-applications-5baff541e826?source=rss----85f9df9eaa17---4","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/a-new-chapter-for-qiskit-algorithms-and-applications-7vnaoyquo","summary":"The Qiskit Ecosystem has undergone changes to provide the community with a greater role in algorithm and application development. The algorithms have been moved to an independent package, and the applications repositories have been relocated. External partners have become maintainers of the repositories. Legacy dependencies have been cleaned up to simplify the code base.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/1cbcbae14e0ae65ad235bb66e5f18fb0?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-11-27T13:01:48.819Z"},{"id":"BltlQ2caC","title":"Quantum Glasses, a Qiskit Ecosystem package for Bloch sphere simulations","url":"https://medium.com/qiskit/quantum-glasses-a-qiskit-ecosystem-package-for-bloch-sphere-simulations-f443698bbb98?source=rss----85f9df9eaa17---4","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/quantum-glasses-a-qiskit-ecosystem-package-for-bloch-sphere-simulations-bltlq2cac","summary":"Quantum Glasses is a Qiskit Ecosystem package that provides a GUI-based tool for visualizing Bloch spheres and understanding quantum computing concepts. It supports 11 single-qubit gates and allows users to apply a series of gates to see the impact on a qubit. However, it is limited to a single qubit and cannot visualize concepts like quantum entanglement. Future work aims to address these limitations and improve the functionality of the app.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/b5b2d8aa434092c709cdab73f224933e?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-11-15T15:56:43.081Z"},{"id":"FKEWOFVeV","title":"Qiskit v0.45 is here!","url":"https://medium.com/qiskit/qiskit-v0-45-is-here-69e861fbfc88?source=rss----85f9df9eaa17---4","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/qiskit-v0-45-is-here--fkewofvev","summary":"Qiskit v0.45 introduces new features such as the passmanager sub-module, improved workflow for transpiler layout, and the SabrePreLayout pass. It also includes performance improvements in transpilation and circuit construction. The release also deprecates the qiskit.extensions sub-module and introduces breaking changes with the removal of deprecated code.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/9c742e19d218224b59b2ea7f4aad89a4?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-11-06T15:31:57.041Z"},{"id":"newukyTPq","title":"Enhance variational quantum algorithms with Qiskit Pulse and Qiskit Dynamics","url":"https://medium.com/qiskit/enhance-variational-quantum-algorithms-with-qiskit-pulse-and-qiskit-dynamics-768249daf8dd?source=rss----85f9df9eaa17---4","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/enhance-variational-quantum-algorithms-with-qiskit-pulse-and-qiskit-dynamics-newukytpq","summary":"Explore how to enhance variational quantum algorithms with Qiskit Pulse and Qiskit Dynamics. Learn about the Parameterized Quantum Pulse Circuit and its potential benefits for running VQA algorithms on near-term quantum hardware.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/d5e6c242c828dde63dfd72e9df28c40b?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-11-01T14:23:29.154Z"},{"id":"CVfAxFmWb","title":"Schr\u00f6dinger\u2019s cat meets Qiskit: Why do we never see cats that are both dead and alive?","url":"https://medium.com/qiskit/schr%C3%B6dingers-cat-meets-qiskit-why-do-we-never-see-cats-that-are-both-dead-and-alive-6e9adf7a09e0?source=rss----85f9df9eaa17---4","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/schr-dinger-s-cat-meets-qiskit-why-do-we-never-see-cats-that-are-both-dead-and-alive--cvfaxfmwb","summary":"The article explores Schr\u00f6dinger's cat thought experiment, which demonstrates the concept of superposition in quantum mechanics. It discusses the collapse postulate, different theories in quantum mechanics, and the emergence of classicality through decoherence. The article also touches upon the application of quantum computing in modeling Schr\u00f6dinger's cat states.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/00ca72b7c5a5250e27cfec283ad7bf04?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-10-25T14:26:01.019Z"}],"similar_hand